  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342247",
      "title": "How Deno Features Are Organized",
      "lectureOrder": 524,
      "videoOrder": 465,
      "sourceHash": "afc68b3a5620daa024bcf86a4571f5d694fd1fed73a13bb8043f6df53f192e50",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "So we got started with Deno here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 8.95,
          "en": "we wrote some first basic Deno code to get good IDE support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.95,
          "end": 11.63,
          "en": "Again, I'll switch back to the extensions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.63,
          "end": 13.88,
          "en": "And there I'm just going to enable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.88,
          "end": 16.35,
          "en": "my Deno extension again here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.35,
          "end": 20.5,
          "en": "And with that done, we can continue with development here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.5,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "Let's now dig a bit deeper into Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "And for that, it's important to understand how Deno code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 30.13,
          "en": "and features are being organized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.13,
          "end": 34.22,
          "en": "We get those core APIs, the so called Namespace APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.22,
          "end": 37.57,
          "en": "Which are built-in core functionalities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.57,
          "end": 39.68,
          "en": "built-in utility functions as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.68,
          "end": 44.68,
          "en": "like set timeout, like right file, so all these core APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.95,
          "end": 48.85,
          "en": "which you can see here in those docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.85,
          "end": 51.913,
          "en": "These are core APIs built into Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.08,
          "end": 55.58,
          "en": "Now, we also got the Standard Library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.58,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "which is a set of modules which you have to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "into your files in order to use them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 65.32,
          "en": "but which are still being maintained by the Deno team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.32,
          "end": 67.79,
          "en": "And then we got third party libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.79,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "which are maintained by the community.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.75,
          "end": 74.84,
          "en": "Now, the Deno Namespace APIs are stable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.84,
          "end": 77.14,
          "en": "so they shouldn't really change anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.14,
          "end": 79.58,
          "en": "And they are maintained by the core team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.58,
          "end": 81.23,
          "en": "The Standard Library modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.23,
          "end": 83.51,
          "en": "are also maintained by the team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.51,
          "end": 85.97,
          "en": "But they're not necessarily stable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.97,
          "end": 90.91,
          "en": "They're some things some features could still change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.91,
          "end": 93.86,
          "en": "For third party libraries, as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.86,
          "end": 96.88,
          "en": "those are maintained by different community teams,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.88,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "not by the official Deno team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 102.19,
          "en": "and therefore their stability and maturity also differs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.19,
          "end": 105.25,
          "en": "Some libraries are very new, some libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.25,
          "end": 108.32300000000001,
          "en": "are heavily maintained and might be quite stable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.25,
          "end": 113.45,
          "en": "Now the Namespace APIs are built into Deno, no installation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.45,
          "end": 117.61,
          "en": "no imports are required to use those features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.61,
          "end": 120.013,
          "en": "as you see here, with our right file extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.69,
          "end": 123.18,
          "en": "And that, of course is a difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.18,
          "end": 126.89,
          "en": "compared to the Node core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.89,
          "end": 130.65,
          "en": "For those core APIs like the file system API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 134.77,
          "en": "we of course needed to add an import to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.77,
          "end": 137.55,
          "en": "That's a difference for these core Deno features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.55,
          "end": 139.113,
          "en": "no import is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.18,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "But if we then move a step further",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 146.06,
          "en": "towards the Standard Library, we will need to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.06,
          "end": 148.28,
          "en": "those modules in order to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.28,
          "end": 150.52,
          "en": "We still don't need to install anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.52,
          "end": 153.02,
          "en": "But as you will see, installation is not really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.02,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "a thing in Deno scripts anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 158.81,
          "en": "but we'll need to import those libraries to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.81,
          "end": 160.37,
          "en": "That brings up the question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.37,
          "end": 161.92000000000002,
          "en": "what is the Standard Library?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.92000000000002,
          "end": 163.663,
          "en": "And what's the node equivalent?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.54,
          "end": 167.14,
          "en": "Well, we can find out more about the Standard Library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.14,
          "end": 171.54,
          "en": "on the Deno page, Deno.land,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.54,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "and then there you find the Standard Library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 176.97,
          "en": "And these are simply a bunch of packages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.97,
          "end": 180.63,
          "en": "which in the end build up on the core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.63,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "And make certain things easier to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 186.2,
          "en": "You could build any kind of app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.2,
          "end": 189.4,
          "en": "with just a core runtime API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.4,
          "end": 193.72,
          "en": "But it gets easier if you use some Standard Library modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.72,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "or even also some third party modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 200.42000000000002,
          "en": "which build up on those core APIs to make certain things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.42000000000002,
          "end": 203.69,
          "en": "like listening to incoming requests easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.69,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "And that's the whole idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "The Standard Library builds up on those core APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.683,
          "en": "and makes working with those APIs easier, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.92000000000002,
          "end": 215.54,
          "en": "Third party libraries have the same idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.54,
          "end": 217.82,
          "en": "There you also don't need to install anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.82,
          "end": 219.76,
          "en": "but you need to import them to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.76,
          "end": 222.38,
          "en": "And they also build up on the core APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.38,
          "end": 226.92000000000002,
          "en": "So those Namespace or runtime APIs are built into Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.92000000000002,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "And they have a small set of low level core functionalities",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 233.84,
          "en": "with which you could build everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.84,
          "end": 236.39,
          "en": "but doing so would be cumbersome, that's why we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.39,
          "end": 239.29,
          "en": "the Standard Library and third party libraries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.29,
          "end": 243.68,
          "en": "The third party modules that build up on those core APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.68,
          "end": 248.57,
          "en": "to make the integration of certain features easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.57,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "And therefore, let's now make the next logical step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 256.27,
          "en": "And let's start using some Standard Library features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.27,
          "end": 260.42,
          "en": "as this will also cover one important aspect of Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.42,
          "end": 264.78,
          "en": "It will show you how we integrate our modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 266.633,
          "en": "into our Deno code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
